  pi(A) = 0.3226
  pi(C) = 0.1068
  pi(G) = 0.1376
  pi(T) = 0.4331

Rate matrix Q:

  A   -0.6327   0.03533     0.219    0.3783
  C    0.1067    -2.522   0.05631     2.358
  G    0.5135    0.0437   -0.8341     0.277
  T    0.2818    0.5814     0.088   -0.9512

Model of rate heterogeneity: Gamma with 4 categories
Gamma shape alpha: 0.3784

 Category  Relative_rate  Proportion
  1         0.01373        0.25
  2         0.1655         0.25
  3         0.7068         0.25
  4         3.114          0.25
Relative rates are computed as MEAN of the portion of the Gamma distribution falling in the category.

